This is a **link_detach**: mswitch2's eth2 interface has been completely detached from the container. The switch10 side still shows UP/LOWER_UP (cable at that end is still "plugged in"), but the mswitch2 end is gone, so no frames can pass the boundary. Same-subnet (pc15 ↔ pc16) traffic stays within switch10 and never needs the uplink — that's why it works. Any cross-subnet packet requires going through mswitch2.eth2, which no longer exists.

The evidence is direct and unambiguous. Advancing to Phase 5.

