=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: mswitch2
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** Interface eth2 on mswitch2 (the msw2_sw10 uplink connecting mswitch2 to switch10) has been entirely detached (link_detach fault).

**Mechanism:** The switch10-side of the link (switch10.eth0) remains UP/LOWER_UP — it shows as physically connected — but the mswitch2 end (eth2) is completely absent from mswitch2's kernel interface table. As a result, no frames can transit from switch10 into mswitch2. All four hosts on switch10 (pc15, pc16, pc17, pc18, subnet 172.18.51.0/24) are isolated from every cross-subnet destination because all inter-subnet traffic must transit mswitch2. Within switch10 itself, hosts can still communicate via switch10's local L2 bridge (explaining why pc15 ↔ pc16 ping succeeds by direct IP at 0% loss).

**Localization:** mswitch2, interface eth2 (collision domain msw2_sw10). The interface is not DOWN — it is entirely missing from `ip link show`, which is the definitive fingerprint of link_detach in Kathara.

**Root cause:** mswitch2's eth2 interface was detached from the container, severing the only uplink between switch10 and mswitch2, and thereby cutting all 172.18.51.x hosts off from the rest of the network.

**Fix:** Re-attach mswitch2's eth2 interface to the msw2_sw10 collision domain (reconnect the virtual cable between mswitch2 and switch10 in the Kathara lab configuration), restoring L2 connectivity from the switch10 subnet to mswitch2 and full cross-subnet routing for pc15–pc18.
=== END ===